{"In vital/lib/reschedule.ts, wipemycalother/lib/reschedule.ts, handleCancelBooking.ts, and the trpc bookings router, async callbacks are passed to Array.forEach, causing all returned promises to be discarded and errors to be silently swallowed. Calendar and video deletion/update operations are fire-and-forget, leaving external integrations in inconsistent state.": 0.9861429333686829, "getCalendar was changed to async (returning Promise<Calendar | null>), but getCalendarCredentials in CalendarManager.ts still calls it synchronously, embedding an unresolved Promise in returned objects. Callers that do not await the result will operate on a Promise instead of a Calendar instance, causing silent logic bugs.": 0.972251832485199, "Dynamic import returns a Promise that resolves to a module namespace, changing the runtime contract of appStore from a module object to a Promise that needs awaiting. Callers forgetting to await will get unexpected behavior.": 0.7487373948097229, "Dynamic imports can split bundles and change startup performance and cold-start behavior - need to ensure this is intended.": 0.19412800669670105, "Dynamic imports may affect how bundlers include/exclude code for tree-shaking and dead code elimination.": 0.06914981454610825, "Synchronous import of appStore combined with dynamic imports creates a dependency chain that can produce circular dependency issues at runtime when app modules import back into core packages.": 0.37588563561439514}